# Archives and stray media — build the zip from a clean checkout instead
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.mp4
*.mov

# Public corpora downloaded into the repo root. IAM_dataset is 1.4 GB of word
# images and reached a commit once, via `git add -A`, taking .git from 30 MB to
# 1.2 GB. It is redownloadable and belongs outside version control.
/IAM_dataset/
/GNHK_dataset/

# Datasets and generated pages — never in history. The corpus is redownloaded
# from Kaggle and the synthetic pages are regenerated from their seeds.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `data/` also matches the source
# package `backend/app/data/`, and silently drops corpus.py, augment.py and
# dataset.py from every commit.
/backend/data/
/data/

# Trained weights. resnet18 alone is 129 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB file limit,
# and every checkpoint is reproducible with `python -m app.train`. The run's
# results.json, eval.json, robustness.json and metrics.csv ARE committed:
# they are the evidence the deck quotes, and they are small.
*.ckpt

# Compiled notes and the fine-tune log are user data, not source.
/vault/
/backend/runs_real/
/backend/runs_real.log

# The live feed palimtop tails. Pure runtime chatter: it rotates, it is
# rewritten whenever it grows, and it says nothing a reader of the repo needs.
# history.csv is the opposite and is deliberately NOT here: it is the learning
# curve across runs and the only record that survives them.
/backend/runs/activity.jsonl
/backend/runs_distil/

# Internal working notes and tooling — not part of the submission.
/track.md
/design/
/.tastemaker/
/docs/superpowers/
